## 📏 Standing Rules (apply to every part of this prompt)

```
RULE 1 — OPTIMIZED CODE: No redundant logic, no duplicate API calls, no re-fetching
data that's already in state. Reuse existing services/components wherever one already
exists instead of writing a parallel version.

RULE 2 — STRUCTURED CODE: Every file has one clear responsibility. Components stay
presentational; validation/business logic lives in hooks or services, not inline in
JSX. Backend follows the existing routes → controllers → services layering exactly.

RULE 3 — MODERN, CLEAR UI/UX: Every interactive element (checkboxes, pills, textarea,
CTA) uses the existing white + #F50A70 design tokens, real transition/hover states,
and clear visual feedback (progress %, live counters, disabled states) — never a
static, unresponsive UI.

RULE 4 — FULL STACK CONNECTION: Every checkbox, selector, and counter must reflect
REAL data from MongoDB via the real API — no local-only UI state that isn't persisted.
Checklist state must survive a page refresh because it's actually saved server-side.

RULE 5 — THESE RULES ARE PART OF THE OUTPUT CONTRACT: The AI must self-check against
all 5 rules in its final summary, not just silently apply them.
```

